": 0.671, "bm25": 14.22, "dense_rank": 7, "bm25_rank": 6, "rrf": 0.03008, "selected": false}, {"text": "Despite Webb's mirror diameter being 2.7 times larger than that of the Hubble Space Telescope, it produces images of comparable resolution because it observes i", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.679, "bm25": 11.16, "dense_rank": 6, "bm25_rank": 17, "rrf": 0.02814, "selected": false}, {"text": "In January 2022, it arrived at its destination, a solar orbit near the Sun\u2013Earth L2 Lagrange point, about 1.5 million kilometers (930,000 mi) from Earth. The te", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.643, "bm25": 11.06, "dense_rank": 8, "bm25_rank": 18, "rrf": 0.02753, "selected": false}], "selected": 3, "echo_filtered": 1, "kept": 2}, "t": 7.342}
