{"status": "progress", "message": "Retrieved 147 candidate paragraphs; kept 3", "stage": "retrieve", "claim_index": 2, "data": {"kind": "retrieval", "pass": 1, "queries": ["James Webb Space Telescope", "European Space Agency"], "candidates": 147, "by_source": {"arxiv": 6, "wikipedia": 141}, "avgdl": 115.5, "top": [{"text": "In January 2022, it arrived at its destination, a solar orbit near the Sun\u2013Earth L2 Lagrange point, about 1.5 million kilometers (930,000 mi) from Earth. The te", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.586, "bm25": 13.75, "dense_rank": 2, "bm25_rank": 5, "rrf": 0.03151, "selected": true}, {"text": "He also dealt with the Apollo 1 fire. He helped found the National Academy of Public Administration, a key locus for governmental reform studies. In 2002, the N", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.524, "bm25": 14.65, "dense_rank": 5, "bm25_rank": 3, "rrf": 0.03126, "selected": true}, {"text": "The NASA Goddard Space Flight Center in Maryland managed telescope development, while the Space Telescope Science Institute in Baltimore on the Homewood Campus ", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.559, "bm25": 13.04, "dense_rank": 3, "bm25_rank": 7, "rrf": 0.0308, "selected": true}, {"text": "Webb died from a heart attack at Georgetown University Hospital in Washington on March 27, 1992, at age 85. He was buried in Arlington National Cemetery. NASA's", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.49, "bm25": 14.49, "dense_rank": 9, "bm25_rank": 4, "rrf": 0.03012, "selected": false}, {"text": "In 1997, NASA worked with the Goddard Space Flight Center, Ball Aerospace & Technologies, and TRW to conduct technical requirement and cost studies of the three", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.49, "bm25": 12.42, "dense_rank": 8, "bm25_rank": 8, "rrf": 0.02941, "selected": false}, {"text": "Twenty-six years ago a small committee report, building on earlier studies, expounded a compelling and poetic vision for the future of astronomy, calling for an", "source": "arxiv", "dense": 0.53